---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/ai.css';
---

<Layout
  title="Grok 4.7 — xAI — Rycode"
  description="xAI’s current coding and knowledge-work frontier model. API id grok-4.7."
  variant="ai"
>
  <article class="ai-model">
    <p class="ai-model-kicker">xAI · current</p>
    <h1 class="ai-model-title">Grok 4.7</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">Grok 4.7 is SpaceXAI / xAI’s frontier model for coding, agentic tasks, and knowledge work. API id: <code>grok-4.7</code>. Announce date: 21 Sep 2026. Available in Cursor, Grok Build, the Grok API, and partner harnesses / routers / clouds. Consumer web, mobile, and Grok-in-X: later (model card).</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Training</h2>
    <p>Company: new, larger base model than Grok 4.6; longer reinforcement-learning run on a harder task mix weighted toward multi-hour problems; improved self-verification and long-context management; trained to natively understand the Grok Bot harness. Model card notes supplemental training on anonymized Cursor workflow data. Parameter count, FLOPs, full dataset mix: UNKNOWN on announce and docs (do not use 2.1T rumor posts). Docs overview: knowledge cutoff May 2026. Model card (21 Sep 2026): pretraining data cutoff June 2026; supplemental training uses data generated as late as August 2026. Do not copy Grok 4.6’s Feb 1, 2026 cutoff onto 4.7.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Inference</h2>
    <p>Reasoning efforts: <code>low</code>, <code>medium</code>, <code>high</code> (default), <code>xhigh</code>. Function calling and structured outputs: yes. Modalities: text and image in, text out. Tools on the overview: function calling, web search, X search, code execution. Batch API: not supported. Rate limits (docs): 150 requests/sec; 50,000,000 tokens/min. Regions on the model page: us-east-1, us-west-2, us-central-1. Also served on the US regional endpoint <code>https://us.api.x.ai/v1</code> (10% token premium; fetched 21 Sep 2026).</p>
    <p>Fast variant: same model on faster infrastructure, billed at twice the standard token rates. Live docs: available only in Cursor and Grok Build; not on the public xAI API; not in Grok Build’s free tier. No public API slug listed (not <code>grok-4.7-fast</code> on the models table).</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Context</h2>
    <p>500,000 token context window. No text output limit (overview).</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Methods</h2>
    <p>Configurable reasoning effort. Exact train-time RL recipe beyond announce framing: UNKNOWN.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Benchmarking</h2>
    <p>Vendor scores on the 21 Sep 2026 announce comparison table (vs Grok 4.6, GPT-5.6 Sol, Fable 5.1). Independent third-party leaderboards: UNKNOWN here. Do not invent.</p>
    <div class="ai-model-table-wrap">
      <table class="ai-model-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Benchmark</th>
            <th scope="col">Grok 4.7</th>
            <th scope="col">Grok 4.6</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>CursorBench 4.0</td><td>46.3%</td><td>40.4%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>DeepSWE v1.1</td><td>71.0%*</td><td>65.2%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>EEBench</td><td>64.0%</td><td>53.0%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>AA Briefcase v1.1</td><td>1,657</td><td>1,546</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Terminal-Bench 4.0</td><td>38.0%</td><td>20.3%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Harvey Legal Agent Benchmark</td><td>19.6%</td><td>15.8%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>HealthBench Professional</td><td>56.7%</td><td>48.5%</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>* DeepSWE 4.7 is a high-effort score (announce). GPT-5.6 Sol and Fable 5.1 columns live on the same table; not copied as independent scores.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Hardware</h2>
    <p>Training / serving silicon and cluster size for Grok 4.7: UNKNOWN on announce and model docs. Campus context stays on <a href="/ai/hardware/memphis-colossus/">Memphis / Colossus</a> when published, not invented here.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Access and pricing (vendor)</h2>
    <p>Copied from docs.x.ai, 21 Sep 2026. Per 1M tokens. Long-context tier applies when the prompt is ≥ 200k tokens (higher rate for all tokens in that request).</p>
    <div class="ai-model-table-wrap">
      <table class="ai-model-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Band</th>
            <th scope="col">Input</th>
            <th scope="col">Cached</th>
            <th scope="col">Output</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>&lt; 200k</td><td>$2.00</td><td>$0.50</td><td>$6.00</td></tr>
          <tr><td>≥ 200k</td><td>$4.00</td><td>$1.00</td><td>$12.00</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Grok 4.7 Fast (Cursor and Grok Build only; not public API): twice those rates. Below 200k: $4 / $1 / $12. Above 200k: $6 / $1.50 / $18 (pricing page, 21 Sep 2026).</p>
    <p>Re-check the live models page before you quote a dollar.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Sources</h2>
    <ul class="ai-model-sources">
      <li><a href="https://x.ai/news/grok-4-7">Introducing Grok 4.7</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://docs.x.ai/developers/models/grok-4.7">Docs: Grok 4.7</a> (fetched 21 Sep 2026)</li>
      <li><a href="https://docs.x.ai/developers/grok-4-7">Grok 4.7 overview</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://docs.x.ai/developers/models">Models index</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://docs.x.ai/developers/pricing">Pricing</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://media.x.ai/v1/website/4p7card-5eccc980.pdf">Model Card: Grok 4.7 (PDF)</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>
